  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>z</mi></math> is a complex number such that <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2,</mn></math>&nbsp;then the area (in sq. units) of the triangle whose vertices are given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> points will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Area of the triangle for these points as vertices<math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;sq. units<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Area of triangle&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> sq. units",
